1692: „if still unanswered 14 days after the helper's answer, the helper gets
'Nino is following up your lead' with no fact — an effort never vanishes
without a word." Once a day at 09:00 UTC, an answer whose „how did it go?"
debrief was armed and never answered, with no outcome and no thank-you, gives
the helper that one fixed line in their language, rung once, and a
helper_thanks row in state followed_up (migration 229) so it is said once.
At most 100 a day.

Only answers whose debrief was armed qualify, and the sweep itself returns at
once while ANSWER_DEBRIEF_ON is off: nothing happens until Misho's yes on AV.
The switch moved to answerDebriefSwitch.ts so debrief and helperThanks do not
import each other.

